     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (immediate-release, labeled maximum). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum per dose of about 850 mg to 1,000 mg. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is high, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, please confirm. Add the clinical rationale too, and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
